  "plain": "In the 1950s there was a craze for anti-gravity research in America, and in the 1960s it seemed to simply vanish. According to the physicist Hal Puthoff, either the work went nowhere or it \"went black\", meaning it moved into secret classified programs. Michels passes this on from Puthoff, in a talk that also brings in the mathematician Eric Weinstein. If the second answer is right, anti-gravity work may have gone on in secret."
